      "scope": "Whole process including input read, normalization, sorted-map counting, ranking, printing and teardown. Input generation and compilation excluded. Timings use uninstrumented binaries; fresh-process RSS and fwp managed counters are separate. C/Rust implement only ASCII; input fixtures are ASCII. fwp also accepts UTF-8 text, with ASCII-only lowercasing. All materialize normalized words and use sorted contiguous key/count pairs. String/list layout, allocation growth, sorting and buffering implementations differ. C/Rust combine the three normalization passes; fwp may allocate intermediate strings. Managed counters exclude raw buffers, allocator metadata, stacks and process startup; they are not comparable to whole-process RSS. No C/Rust allocation counts are claimed. Ratios are per-host fwp median / peer median; all samples retained. No timing budget or cross-version improvement is established by this baseline."
